QuaternaryQuartics -- code to support the paper 'Quaternary Quartic Forms and Gorenstein Rings'
***********************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package contains code and examples for the paper *note [QQ]: [QQ],
Quaternary Quartic Forms and Gorenstein Rings, by Grzegorz Kapustka, Michal
Kapustka, Kristian Ranestad, Hal Schenck, Mike Stillman and Beihui Yuan,
referenced below.

We study the space of quartic forms in four variables, interleaving the notions
of: rank, border rank, annihilator of the quartic form, Betti tables, and
Calabi-Yau varieties of codimension 4.



Section 1: Generating the Betti tables
======================================

  * *note Finding the 16 betti tables possible for quartic forms in 4
    variables, and examples: Finding the 16 betti tables possible for quartic
    forms in 4 variables_cm and examples, -- Material from Table 6 and 7 of
    Appendix 1

Section 2: Basic constructions
==============================

  * *note Doubling Examples: Doubling Examples, -- Doubling of each type of set
    of points
  * *note Doubling Examples for ideals of 6 points: Doubling Examples for
    ideals of 6 points, -- For an ideal $I_{\Gamma}$ of six points we compute
    possible doublings of $I_{\Gamma}$. See Example 2.16 in [QQ] for details
  * *note Example Type [300a]: Example Type [300a], -- An example of an apolar
    ideal of a quartic that cannot be obtained as a doubling of it's apolar set
  * *note Example Type [300b]: Example Type [300b], -- An example of doubling
    construction
  * *note Example Type [300c]: Example Type [300c], -- The third family of type
    [300]

Section 3: betti tables for points in P^3 with given geometry
=============================================================

  * *note Finding the possible betti tables for points in P^3 with given
    geometry: Finding the possible betti tables for points in P^3 with given
    geometry, -- Material from Section 3 of [QQ]

Section 4: the quadratic part of the apolar ideal
=================================================

  * *note Finding all possible betti tables for quadratic component of inverse
    system for quartics in 4 variables: Finding all possible betti tables for
    quadratic component of inverse system for quartics in 4 variables, --
    Material from Section 4 of [QQ]

Section 5: VSP(F,9) for a general quadric form of rank 9
========================================================

  * *note VSP(F_Q,9): VSP_lpF_usQ_cm9_rp, -- Computation appearing in the proof
    of Theorem 5.16 in [QQ]

Section 6: Stratification of the space of quaternary quartics
=============================================================

  * *note Finding the Betti stratum of a given quartic: Finding the Betti
    stratum of a given quartic, -- the 19 Betti strata
  * *note Noether-Lefschetz examples: Noether-Lefschetz examples, -- examples
    from Section 6.2 in [QQ]

Section 7: Codimension three varieties in quadrics
==================================================

  * *note Pfaffians on quadrics: Pfaffians on quadrics, -- compute the quartic
    and betti table corresponding to a pfaffian ideal in a quadric

Section 8: Irreducible liftings
===============================

  * *note Type [000], CY of degree 20: Type [000]_cm CY of degree 20, --
    lifting to a 3-fold with two singular points
  * *note Singularities of lifting of type [300b]: Singularities of lifting of
    type [300b], -- The lifting of [300b] defined by biliaison acquires
    singularities in dimension 3
  * *note Half canonical degree 20: Half canonical degree 20, -- Computation
    which supports the proof of Proposition 8.4

