Get inverse system of all degree d polynomials in k variables, by taking sums
of n monomials. By taking sufficiently many monomials we'll get everything.
Work over Z/2 for speed, experiments suggest that even over Z/2 we get all
betti tables. If inverse system has a linear generator, ignore it. Pack results
using netlist for pretty display. For k=4=d, we get 16 betti tables by using
n=4 terms.

