nondegenerateBorels -- construct all nondegenerate strongly stable ideals of given length
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        nondegenerateBorels(d, S)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the length of the desired
        ideals in S$
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a polynomial ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Sort => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, whether to sort the generators of each ideal in a slightly more
        natural way
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of all strongly stable ideals in $S$
        which are saturated, are (affine) dimension one, have degree $d$, and
        have no linear forms in their ideal

Description
===========

This is a simplified interface to the *note stronglyStableIdeals:
(StronglyStableIdeals)stronglyStableIdeals, function.



For example, the following are all of the strongly stable ideals with degree 7,
and their Betti tables.

