Type [000], CY of degree 20 -- lifting to a 3-fold with two singular points
***************************************************************************

We construct a singular Calabi-Yau of dimension 3 with 2 nodes, of codimension
4, of degree 20.  This example cannot be smoothed.  However, there is the
example of the determinantal ($3 \times 3$ minors of a $4 \times 4$ matrix of
linear forms, which is a smooth Calabi-Yau 3-fold of degree 20.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : kk = ZZ/31                                                   |
|                                                                  |
|o1 = kk                                                           |
|                                                                  |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                                 |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : U = kk[y0,y1,y2,y3,y4,y5,y6,y7];                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : setRandomSeed 8327432                                        |
| -- setting random seed to 8327432                                |
|                                                                  |
|o3 = 8327432                                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : U1 = vars U                                                  |
|                                                                  |
|o4 = | y0 y1 y2 y3 y4 y5 y6 y7 |                                  |
|                                                                  |
|             1      8                                             |
|o4 : Matrix U  <-- U                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : P6 = matrix{{y1,y2,y3,y4,y5,y6,y7}} -- The hyperplane y0 == 0|
|                                                                  |
|o5 = | y1 y2 y3 y4 y5 y6 y7 |                                     |
|                                                                  |
|             1      7                                             |
|o5 : Matrix U  <-- U                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

